## 5. Security Requirements
- Use PDO prepared statements for all database queries.
- Use PHP password hashing and verification functions.
- Regenerate the session ID after successful login.
- Enable session cookie security settings where supported.
- Protect state-changing forms against CSRF attacks.
- Escape output with `htmlspecialchars()` to prevent XSS.
- Validate all user input on the server.
- Restrict profile access to the logged-in user.
- Use generic login and password-reset responses where appropriate.
- Never commit database credentials or secrets to a public repository.
- Do not use deprecated PHP functions.
- Do not store passwords or reset tokens in plain text.

